# Agent skills manifest — the single declarative source for which skills get
# installed where. Consumers apply it per platform; this file is only the list.
#
# Columns (whitespace-separated; args = everything after method):
#   layer   team | personal | mac
#   method  npx  — `npx -y skills add -g -y <args>`
#           curl — `<name> <url>`: fetch <url> to ~/.agents/skills/<name>/SKILL.md
#   args    method-specific (see above)
#
# Layers:
#   team      baked into iv-image (vendor-skills.sh vendors these at a pinned
#             dotfiles commit); dotfiles installs them on macOS only — Linux VMs
#             get them from the image.
#   personal  dotfiles-only, installed on every machine by install.sh.
#   mac       dotfiles-only, macOS only, NOT vendored into iv-image. For skills
#             that are meaningless on a Linux VM. `npx` args of `.` install from
#             this repo (install.sh runs npx from $DOTFILES_DIR).
#
# Consumers: install.sh setup_agents (macOS: team+personal+mac, Linux:
# personal); iv-image vendor-skills.sh (team). Checked by diff-provisioning.sh
# and by test-install.sh provisioning (manifest vs what is on disk).

team npx matsonj/mviz
team npx vercel-labs/skills -s find-skills
team npx duckdb/duckdb-skills
team npx motherduckdb/agent-skills
team npx posit-dev/skills -s quarto-authoring brand-yml
team npx marimo-team/skills -s marimo-notebook marimo-batch
# herdr: teaches agents to drive herdr from inside a herdr pane (inspect/split
# panes, run without stealing focus, start helper agents). No-ops unless
# HERDR_ENV=1. Team: agents run in herdr on VMs too (iv-image re-vendors it).
team npx ogulcancelik/herdr -s herdr
# tailscale: Tailscale's own skill (alpha, tailscale/tailscale-skill). Team,
# because the fleet's tailnet is a provisioning concern, not a personal one:
# every VM joins in provision-iv.sh, and the failures are policy-file and
# auth-key shaped -- tagOwners, OAuth scopes, `tag:dev` vs the exe.dev `tailnet`
# tag. Those cost most of a debugging cycle on 2026-08-23 (see
# exeslim/iv-tailnet-join.sh) because the answer lived in Tailscale's docs and
# nothing on the VM carried them.
#
# NOTE it is the vendor's own skill, so what it teaches is upstream's model, NOT
# this fleet's. It does not know about `api-tailscale`, the edge-injected
# credential, or the join path in provision-iv.sh -- tailnet.md and the
# join-tailnet skill remain the authority on those, and this skill's generic
# `tailscale up --auth-key=` advice is wrong here. Kept adjacent rather than
# merged for exactly that reason.
team npx tailscale/tailscale-skill
# archil-guide has no GitHub repo — fetched directly
team curl archil-guide https://archil.com/skill.md

personal npx tigrisdata/tigris-agents-plugins
personal npx marimo-team/marimo-pair
personal npx kylelundstedt/dotfiles -s sprites-dev join-tailnet upgrade-vm exe-dev
# apple-containers is private (macOS-only, this repo) — installed from `.`, not
# published to a skills repo and not vendored into iv-image
mac npx . -s apple-containers
